   "id": "intel-crash",
   "headline": "Intel's weak outlook triggers its worst day in decades",
   "facts": [
    "Shares -28.6% Fri 30 Oct (Reuters); worst day in 50+ years (Decrypt)",
    "Q4 revenue guide $15-16B vs ~$17.1B; adj EPS $0.25 vs $0.43; gross margin guide 38% vs 44.1% Q3",
    "CFO: probably no positive FCF next year; 2027 investment year",
    "Israel fab accident and substrate shortage (single source, TIKR)"
   ],
   "sources": [
    "https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/nasdaq-futures-tumble-as-amazon-intel-results-deepen-ai-spending-woes-4986163",
    "https://decrypt.co/382287/intel-stock-suffers-worst-crash-in-50-years-as-weak-forecast-overshadows-ai-chip-demand",
    "https://www.tikr.com/blog/intel-tumbles-as-israel-fab-shutdown-and-substrate-shortage-hit-q4-guidance"
   ],
   "paragraph": "Gross margin is simply what is left of each sales dollar after paying the direct cost of making the product. Intel guided fourth-quarter gross margin to 38%, down from 44.1% in the third quarter. Revenue guidance was $15 billion to $16 billion against about $17.1 billion expected. Shares closed down 28.6% on 30 October, which Decrypt called the worst one-day drop in more than 50 years. The CFO said positive free cash flow next year is probably not coming, calling 2027 an investment year. Reported causes are an Israel fab shutdown after an accident and a substrate shortage, from a single source. How long either lasts is unknown.",
   "edited": "none",
   "explainer": "sonnet"
  },
  {
   "id": "openai-raise-cut",
   "headline": "OpenAI reportedly cuts its fundraising target to $20 billion",
   "facts": [
    "FT 30 Oct: target cut from ~$30B to ~$20B; pre-money valuation $1.25T from $1.4T",
    "UAE-led; later wealthy-individual offering",
    "WSJ: $11B secured, some investors tepid (single source)",
    "OpenAI no comment"
   ],
   "sources": [
    "https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/10/30/openai-reportedly-cuts-fundraising-target-amid-ai-jitters",
    "https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/31/openai-reportedly-lowers-funding-target-for-new-round/",
    "https://fortune.com/2026/10/31/ai-boom-bust-openai-fundraising-target-meta-credit-warning-cash-flow-capex"
   ],
   "paragraph": "A funding round is a company selling new shares to raise cash, and the price tag is the valuation. The Financial Times reported that OpenAI cut its target from about $30 billion to about $20 billion, and its valuation from $1.4 trillion to $1.25 trillion, counted before the new money goes in. UAE investors lead, and a later offering to wealthy individuals could lift the total to $20 billion. The Wall Street Journal reported $11 billion secured so far, with some large investors tepid, though that is a single source. OpenAI had not commented, every figure is a press report, and the final size and closing date are unknown.",
   "edited": "none",
   "explainer": "sonnet"
  },
  {
   "id": "meta-sp-outlook",
   "headline": "S&P turns its outlook on Meta negative over AI spending",
   "facts": [
    "S&P outlook stable to negative, AA- kept, 30 Oct",
    "Leverage could pass 1.0x by 2027 vs ~0.1x 2025",
    "2026 FOCF deficit conflict: Reuters -$39B, Fortune -$22B; 2027 -$71B",
    "Capex guide $135-145B; Meta disagrees"
   ],
   "sources": [
    "https://kfgo.com/2026/10/30/sp-global-revises-outlook-on-meta-to-negative-on-cashflow-concerns/",
    "https://fortune.com/2026/10/31/ai-boom-bust-openai-fundraising-target-meta-credit-warning-cash-flow-capex"
   ],
   "paragraph": "A credit rating is a grade for how safely a borrower can repay debt, and an outlook is a warning about which way it may move. S&P kept Meta at AA- but changed the outlook from stable to negative, which is not a downgrade. The worry is uncertainty over heavy AI spending: Meta guided capital spending of $135 billion to $145 billion. S&P said leverage could pass its 1.0x threshold as soon as 2027, against about 0.1x in 2025. Meta replied that it respectfully disagrees about its AI monetization capabilities. Whether the spending earns its cost back is the disputed point, and sources conflict on S&P's 2026 deficit forecast.",
   "edited": "none",
   "explainer": "sonnet"
  },
  {
   "id": "apple-qwen-china",
   "headline": "Apple Intelligence comes to China, powered by Alibaba's Qwen",
   "facts": [
    "Announced 31 Oct by Apple China newsroom and Alibaba",
    "Qwen in Siri, Writing Tools, Visual Intelligence",
    "Dev beta 4 Nov; iOS 27.3 in December; iPhone 15 Pro and later",
    "WWDC 2026 new Siri not included; no training on user data; no financial terms; regulator cleared in July"
   ],
   "sources": [
    "https://www.apple.com.cn/newsroom/2026/10/apple-intelligence-features-are-coming-to-users-in-china/",
    "https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-31/Alibaba-s-Qwen-to-integrate-into-Apple-Intelligence-in-landmark-deal-1RHilSeJsbK/p.html",
    "https://thenextweb.com/news/apple-intelligence-china-ios-27-3-alibaba-qwen"
   ],
   "paragraph": "Behind a smart assistant sits a language model, the part that reads and writes text, and for China that part will be Alibaba's Qwen. Apple and Alibaba announced that Apple Intelligence features arrive in China, with Qwen built into Siri, Writing Tools and Visual Intelligence. Developer beta starts 4 November, and public release comes with iOS 27.3 in December for iPhone 15 Pro and later. The new Siri shown at WWDC 2026 is not included. Alibaba says it will not use user requests or responses to train its models. China's internet regulator cleared the arrangement in July. Financial terms are undisclosed, and how the features perform on a different underlying model is untested publicly.",
   "edited": "none",
   "explainer": "sonnet"
